# Design of the exact solving layer · `spec:nrz:cas-solving-design-contract`

This design is owned by NRZ in area nrz. It implements the contracts and delivery order of (`alg:nrz:cas-solving-delivery`): graph-owned solution relations, exact complex coefficients, independently replayed coverage, and the blind general-cubic derivation as the first release acceptance. It specifies future implementation; this document adds no executable capability. The reviewed concept is (`spec:nrz:cas-solving-concept`). No degree-three formula, quadratic formula, named cubic invariant or hand-selected sum of radicals is a producer primitive.

**Decision (Replacement format and admitted arithmetic dependencies)** · `dec:nrz:cas-solving-design-baseline`

The sole new witness format is NRZCAS03. NRZCAS01, NRZCAS02 and all other magic values are rejected before record allocation; there is no compatibility reader, adapter or persisted-consumer migration. The existing 59 primitive meanings retain version 1 and their existing executable field restrictions. New complex polynomial equalities use coeff.identity with explicit maps; no old checker is silently widened under version 1. The complete solving cost policy is logical version 9, with the 18 additional version-1 schemas below. Existing rational and piecewise services remain available under this new format. This explicitly replaces the wire-version decision of (`dec:nrz:cas-piecewise-design-wire-version`) and the backing and dependency decisions of (`dec:nrz:cas-design-rationals`) and (`dec:nrz:cas-design-crate`).

Rational owns a private `num_rational::Ratio<num_bigint::BigInt>` in reduced form; zero is 0/1 and the denominator is positive. Gaussian rational values own `num_complex::Complex<Rational>`, accessed componentwise through fallible operations. The only added direct dependencies are num-integer, num-traits, num-rational and num-complex alongside num-bigint. Dependency versions come from the repository's admitted local dependency route; this design does not invent lockfile bytes or widen network access. num-traits supplies internal identity/conversion vocabulary, never an unmetered public polynomial arithmetic bound. num-integer supplies integer gcd and perfect-power helpers only behind the prepaid wrappers below. No floating operation, external algebra system or external test suite enters exact replay.

## Graph objects and public construction · `sec:nrz:cas-solving-design-graph`

**Definition (Dependency direction and identity)** · `def:nrz:cas-solving-design-dependencies`

All objects inhabit the existing append-only heterogeneous graph. Handles retain store identity, kind and logical serial; neither petgraph indices nor serials are mathematical identity. A payload reference is an earlier dependency, and a draft-local reference must point backward. Evidence is an Application/Proof pointing to its premises and conclusion objects; a solution object never points back to the proof that certifies it. The same syntax may therefore have several proofs without a cycle in its structural key. Nonsemantic indexes, search queues and arithmetic scratch buffers are bounded views over these objects, not alternative authoritative solution stores.

Intern every new immutable mathematical object by kind, full payload, header, binder scope and ordered dependency keys. Canonicalize only explicitly unordered collections: conjunctions, cover members, selected alternatives and solution-set branch members. Coordinates, matrix rows, polynomial variable frames, tower levels, tuple entries, map outputs, premise slots and root-slot assignments retain order. A finite alternative set removes structurally identical entries but does not merge provably equal expressions without equality evidence. Multiplicity is stored in a separate proved profile. Source occurrences and traversal receipts keep the existing non-interned provenance contract. Hashing may accelerate a lookup but equality always compares complete keys.

