The new public graph drafts are `Draft::Solve(SolveDraft)` with one variant per row. The existing model::RootSelection remains the requested algebraic-root selector; the new graph payload is RootSelectionData with SelectionMode, avoiding a public Rust type-name collision. Every child position uses the existing `Reference`; returned values are checked `Handle`s. `SolveDraft` is syntax only and cannot construct an Application, Proof or sealed witness. Read-only `SolveView<'a>` variants expose borrowed payloads and checked handles. No unchecked Rust constructor or public mutable coefficient buffer is added. Arithmetic scratch polynomials can be materialized as canonical graph Polynomial/CoefficientValue nodes only through the same transaction.

