Graph-kind tags 16–30 and record tags 13–27 are separate namespaces; neither is derived from the other at runtime. The field order in this table, together with the graph admission rules, is the wire schema. Ordered payload vectors retain order; sets use canonical structural order. CoefficientMap target-kind is 0 CoefficientDomain (one ref) or 1 ScalarAmbient (header ref followed by Field encoding). Domain/value subtypes are 0 Rational, 1 Gaussian, 2 Fraction and 3 Quotient/Tower respectively. Coordinate roles are 0 Coefficient, 1 Unknown, 2 Family. Map modes are 0 Embedding and 1 Specialization. Selection modes are 0 Any, 1 Constrained, 2 Principal and 3 Isolated. Branch subtypes are 0 Finite, 1 Image, 2 Algebraic, 3 Empty and 4 Local. Neighborhood modes are 0 Existential and 1 Explicit. Optional metadata is present only for the subtype that needs it; an irrelevant convention or interval is noncanonical and rejected.

Extend existing AmbientDomain encoding by tag 4 Product followed by its CoordinateSpace ref; existing tags 0–3 retain meaning. RegionExpr retains tags 0–6 because GuardTrue/GuardFalse already provide parameter predicates. Operator tags 43 Conjugate, 44 RealPart and 45 ImagPart have one scalar operand; tag 46 RootValue has a u32 slot; tag 47 ExactCoefficient has no operator payload. NRZCAS03 adds an attachment field to every Expression record after its ordinary operand vector: tag 0 None, tag 1 SelectedRoot followed by its selection ref, or tag 2 ExactCoefficient followed by value ref and map ref. RootValue requires attachment 1, ExactCoefficient requires attachment 2, and all other operators require attachment 0. Both new attached literals have no ordinary operands. Field and Branch encodings retain their existing variants; new coefficient domains do not masquerade as a new Field enum value. SolveStatement is outer statement tag 25 with inner tags 0–19 from the statement table; SolveCertificate is outer certificate tag 12 with inner tags 0–17 from the registry. Existing outer statement tags 0–24 and certificate tags 0–11 retain their meanings.

The in-memory Request's stable task discriminant 10 now includes SolveSpec in its canonical request key: problem descriptor, goal byte (0 Candidates, 1 Complete), form byte (0 AnyExact, 1 AlgebraicRoots, 2 Radicals, 3 ExactFamily, 4 LocalBranch) and exclusions byte 0 PreserveOriginal. Requests and traversal receipts are not portable proof records. The witness's SolveProblem and typed conclusion carry the mathematical proposition; the caller reconstructs the expected Coverage/Member/Presentation judgment from its covered Request and compares it during replay. Importing a witness never fabricates an original-source traversal receipt or authorizes a new request without a fresh walk.

